07. firstN=0 → 400
==================
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: REGEX(\d+)

{
  "detail": "'firstN' must be a positive integer (got '0')",
  "status": 400,
  "title": "Invalid request",
  "type": "https://uri.etsi.org/ngsi-ld/errors/BadRequestData"
}



08. offsetN=-1 → 400
====================
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: REGEX(\d+)

{
  "detail": "'offsetN' must be a non-negative integer (got '-1')",
  "status": 400,
  "title": "Invalid request",
  "type": "https://uri.etsi.org/ngsi-ld/errors/BadRequestData"
}



09. firstN=2&lastN=3 → 400 (contradictory directions)
=====================================================
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
Date: REGEX(.*)
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: REGEX(\d+)

{
  "detail": "?firstN= and ?lastN= cannot be combined (ascending vs descending temporal pagination)",
  "status": 400,
  "title": "Invalid request",
  "type": "https://uri.etsi.org/ngsi-ld/errors/BadRequestData"
}



--TEARDOWN--
swBrokerStop
swDbDrop
psql -h localhost -p 5432 -U postgres -c "DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS sw_troe_partial" >/dev/null 2>&1
